        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "cf4dd770-dbb0-5431-b6f1-15dd4b420a93",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Benny Andersson, Björn Ulvaeus\n- Organizations: ABBA\n- Products: \"Money, Money, Money\", \"That's Me\", Arrival, \"Chess\", \"Kristina från Duvemåla\", \"Mamma Mia!\"\n- Places: Japan\n- Topics: songwriting, single releases, chart performance\n\nFacts:\n- Benny Andersson was born on 16 December 1946.\n- Benny Andersson is a Swedish musician and composer who was a member of ABBA from 1972 to 1982.\n- Benny Andersson co-composed the musicals \"Chess\", \"Kristina från Duvemåla\", and \"Mamma Mia!\".\n- ABBA recorded the song \"Money, Money, Money\".\n- Benny Andersson and Björn Ulvaeus wrote \"Money, Money, Money\".\n- In the year following its original release, \"That's Me\" was released as a single in Japan with \"Money, Money, Money\" as the B-side to promote ABBA's album Arrival.\n- In Japan, \"That's Me\" reached number 75 on the official Japanese charts.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
